INT. CONVERTED BOWLING ALLEY - OPEN OFFICE - DAY

Lanes carpeted over. Desks sit where pins used to stand. The ball return hums.

GRETCHEN VOSS (50s, headset, power blazer) paces the gutter. BIG DAVE MUNOZ (40s, linebacker build, lanyard) hunches over a keyboard. PRIYA NAIR (late 20s, three monitors) types without blinking. LEOPOLD ASHFORD (60s, bowtie) polishes a trophy no one has won. HANNELORE BRANDT (30s, cardigan, furious calm) stares at a spreadsheet. TOBY OYELARAN (20s, intern, backward cap) holds a clipboard like a shield.

She stops. Nobody looks up.

GRETCHEN
Quarterly synergy.

Dave stands. Sits. Priya's typing slows, then quickens. Leopold sets down the trophy.

LEOPOLD
We are on track.

GRETCHEN
Are we.

Hannelore turns her monitor ninety degrees. A red cell glows. Toby takes a half step toward the exit. Gretchen catches it.

GRETCHEN (CONT'D)
Toby.

TOBY
Yes, Ms. Voss.

GRETCHEN
Coffee.

He bolts. Dave watches him go, envious.

DAVE
I could use one too.

GRETCHEN
You could use a lot of things.

Priya's keyboard stops. Silence. The ball return clunks.

PRIYA
The numbers are final.

HANNELORE
They are not final.

PRIYA
They are final.

Leopold lifts the trophy again and begins to polish with great concentration. Gretchen crosses to Hannelore, leans over, and reads the red cell. She exhales through her nose.

GRETCHEN
Fix it.

HANNELORE
It's not broken.

GRETCHEN
Then make it less true.

Hannelore picks up a pen. Clicks it. Clicks it again. Dave rolls his chair six inches away from her. Toby returns with six coffees balanced in a cardboard tray, and nobody takes one.
